  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-A 704.01 New Hampshire Residents: Program Options.\n\n(a) Upon conviction under RSA 265-A:2 or RSA 265-A:3, and pursuant to RSA 265-A:42 and RSA 265-A:39, I, a person who is a resident of the state of New Hampshire shall attend one of the following programs if the person wishes to have his or her driver’s license reinstated:\n\n(1) The IDIP closest to the client’s place of residence;\n\n(2) The IDIP closest to the client’s place of permanent employment; or\n\n(3) The WIDIP closest to the client’s place of residence.\n\n(b) If the chosen program is unable to enroll the client within 30 days of sentencing, the client may choose to attend any other IDIP or WIDIP in any catchment area of his or her choice.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at part heading for He-A 704) #4652, eff 7-25-89; ss by #6078, INTERIM, eff 8-21-95, EXPIRED 12-19-95\n\nNew. #6653, EMERGENCY, eff 12-12-97, EXPIRED 4-11-98\n\nNew. #6753, eff 5-20-98; ss by #8624, INTERIM, eff 5-20-06, EXPIRES: 11-16-06; ss by #8749, eff 11-16-06",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-a700.html"
